1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,940
Chat sends the spirits.

2
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:07,020
Your shadow guards the light.

3
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:08,760
This is Khayal:

4
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:10,760
a shadow theatre built for Twitch,

5
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:12,720
where the audience takes the puppets

6
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:15,020
and the streamer steps
inside the performance.

7
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:18,120
The idea comes from
Egyptian shadow theatre:

8
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:19,700
a lamp, a screen,

9
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:22,040
and figures brought to life by people.

10
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:24,440
Khayal brings that shared performance

11
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:26,280
into a stream, with a camera

12
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:28,540
silhouette and puppets
controlled through chat.

13
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,380
A viewer summons a cat

14
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:31,480
or a camel, then

15
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:32,760
moves it with simple commands.

16
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:34,380
Pull it toward the lamp

17
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,420
and the shadow grows larger and softer.

18
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:38,940
Each puppet belongs to one viewer,

19
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:40,560
with a queue when the stage fills.

20
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:42,760
Then comes Afreet Hunt.

21
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:44,020
Sixty seconds.

22
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:45,400
Five lanterns.

23
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:47,520
Chat sends spirits toward the lights

24
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:48,980
while the streamer tries to swat

25
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:50,540
them away with a changing silhouette.

26
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:52,900
Keep at least three lanterns burning

27
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:53,700
to win.

28
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,360
The camera reads movement along

29
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:56,860
your outline, so a still

30
00:00:56,860 --> 00:00:58,080
shadow is not a hit.

31
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,760
A separate cue book lets

32
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:01,200
the streamer direct the show.

33
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:03,420
Rehearsal is clearly labeled,

34
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:05,700
so simulated events stay
separate from Twitch.

35
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:08,900
Captions are cleaned,
commands have cooldowns,

36
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:10,420
and stage moderation stays under

37
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:11,760
the broadcaster's control.

38
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,380
When the curtain falls, a playbill credits

39
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:15,180
the cast.

40
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:17,540
The goal is a small shared performance:

41
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:19,480
an unexpected giant cat,

42
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:21,360
a desperate save, and a record

43
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:22,660
of who helped make the night.

44
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:24,520
I directed the concept

45
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:25,680
and used Codex to build

46
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:28,480
the TypeScript app,
command handling, cue book,

47
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,620
Twitch connection code, and camera worker.

48
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:32,320
Pixi draws the theatre;

49
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:34,140
MediaPipe supplies the silhouette.

50
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:36,940
Tests check the rules, while real camera

51
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:39,160
and Twitch recordings must
prove the performance.

52
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:41,620
Khayal gives chat a part to play

53
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:43,440
and the streamer a stage to inhabit.

54
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:44,840
Bring your shadow.

55
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:47,000
Guard the light. Come back tomorrow.

56
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:48,280
There is more to see.
